TEXT -192 0 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=1m abstol=1m reltol=0.001
TEXT -192 32 Left 2 !.tran 0 1 0 0.1m
TEXT -16 16 Left 2 ;Energy=L*I*I (ALT/(ALT Gr)+Click before CTRL+Click)\n ( NOTE: ALT+click on german keyboard layout often crash LTspice\nPlease use ALT Gr + Click for german keyboards )
TEXT -72 144 Left 2 ;L=4/314.159\nIrms=57400\nHINT: Energy is always ALT/(ALT Gr)+Click before CTRL+Click\nE1=L*I^2=41.95MJ (Can also be integrated by Ix(U2:L1_1)*V(n002) from 984.68ms to 989.68ms = Halfewave of the power)\nE2=L*(0.5I)^2=10.5MJ\nE3=E2\nE=E1+0.5E1=1.5E1=62.9MJ (big amount of energy \n  saved in net inductance at short circuit fault)
TEXT -192 24 Left 2 !.param RN=0.4 RN1=1u LN={4/314.159} LN1=1u
TEXT -200 152 Left 2 ;Also look at \ninductive_energy.wxmx
TEXT -24 112 Left 2 ;SK=short circuit reactive power\nabout 40GVA (XN=4ohm)
TEXT 152 192 Left 2 ;Inner Energy of inductance: L*Ipeak*Ipeak/2=L*Irms*Irms can also be plotted:\nIx(U2:L2_1)*Ix(U2:L2_1)*4/314.159*1J/1A/1A/2\nIx(U2:L3_1)*Ix(U2:L3_1)*4/314.159*1J/1A/1A/2\nIx(U2:L1_1)*Ix(U2:L1_1)*4/314.159*1J/1A/1A/2\nAt maximum phase1 = 41.9MJ\nphase 2=phase3=10.5MJ\nThe sum of inner energy for the three phases of the inductance \nis always the same (approx.63MJ) for each timepoint \n(after transients are done)\nThe energy from/to the voltagesource and impedance\nsums at each timepoint to zero although energy is exchanged\nInductive delivers at each timepoint same amount of\nenergy what it gets from the voltage source
TEXT 112 128 Left 2 ;NOTE: The frequency of power is 100Hz since U,J have 90degrees phaseshift
TEXT -192 240 Left 2 ;For a more in deepth view for the energy \nto/from the inductance from/to the voltage\nsource you can integrate every 2.5ms of\nV(N002)*Ix(U2:L1_1)*1W/1V/1A\nV(N004)*Ix(U2:L2_1)*1W/1V/1A\nV(N006)*Ix(U2:L3_1)*1W/1V/1A\nstarted from 369.67ms
TEXT -192 312 Left 2 ;e.g: 369.67ms-372.17ms: (I phase1 has it's max=inner energy of phase1 has it's max)\nNOTE: all int() values are STRG+Clicked and means  the energy exchange from/to inductance\nL1(inner energy)=Ix(U2:L1_1)*Ix(U2:L1_1)*4/314.159*1J/1A/1A/2)=42MJ to 21MJ \nL1(exchange)=Int(V(N002)*Ix(U2:L1_1)*1W/1V/1A)=-21MJ=Difference of 42MJ and 21MJ \nL2(inner energy)=Ix(U2:L2_1)*Ix(U2:L2_1)*4/314.159*1J/1A/1A/2)=10.6MJ to 2.6MJ \nL2(exchange)=Int(V(N004)*Ix(U2:L2_1)*1W/1V/1A)=-8MJ=Difference of 10.6MJ and 2.6MJ \nL3(inner energy)=Ix(U2:L3_1)*Ix(U2:L3_1)*4/314.159*1J/1A/1A/2)=10MJ to 39MJ \nL3(exchange)=Int(V(N006)*Ix(U2:L3_1)*1W/1V/1A)=29MJ=Difference of 10MJ und 39MJ\nYou can also see that he sum of energy between voltage source and inductance\nis zero -21MJ-8MJ+29MJ=0 for each timepoint\nand the inner energy of the inductance remains unchanged for each timepoint\n42J+10.5J+10.5J=63MJ\nand \n21MJ+3MJ+39MJ=63MJ\nThis is also true for other timesteps:\ne.g. 372.17ms-374.67ms and so on
